<title>FINLAND: AKERHOLM SEES FEW PAN-EUROPEAN BANKS IN EMU.</title>
<headline>AKERHOLM SEES FEW PAN-EUROPEAN BANKS IN EMU.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>There will be only a few pan-European banks after the Economic and Monetary Union has changed the banking environment, Finnish finance ministry under-secretary of state Johnny Akerholm said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;On the other hand there will be more opportunities for entities operating in limited geographical areas whose competitiveness is based on regional know-how,&quot; Akerholm said in a summary of a speech at a seminar arranged by the Finnish Export Credit (FEC) in Singapore.</p>
<p>&quot;There will also be opportunities for specialty financers, which concentrate on a narrow field of expertise,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0248</p>
</text>
